gQB(){return"Mind Engine"},
gRl(){return"Coming soon"},
gux(){return"Minesweeper"},
gut(){return"Eclipse"},
gun(){return"Balance Puzzle"},
guE(){return"Snapshot"},
guA(){return"Rewind"},
guu(){return"What Changed?"},
guq(){return"Constellation"},
guw(){return"Mental Math"},
guo(){return"Block Smash"},
gus(){return"Cube Counter"},
guF(){return"Star Battle"},
gum(){return"2048"},
guy(){return"Numberlink"},
guz(){return"Picross"},
guG(){return"Sudoku"},
gLj(){return"Fill the grid so every row, every column and every box holds each digit exactly once. On Easy the grid is 4x4, with 2x2 boxes and the digits 1 to 4. On the other levels it's 9x9, with 3x3 boxes and the digits 1 to 9.\n\n[fig:sudokuUnits] On a 4x4 grid, the ringed row, column and box each hold 1, 2, 3 and 4, once each.\n\nSo a digit can never appear twice in a row, a column or a box. If it repeats, it turns red.\n\n[fig:sudokuRepeat] Two 3s in the same row: not allowed. A 3 and a 1: allowed.\n\nTo make progress, look for a cell where only one digit is left: all the others are already in its row, its column or its box.\n\n[fig:sudokuSingle] The ringed cell sees a 1 in its row, a 2 in its column and a 4 in its box (shaded cells): it can only be a 3.\n\nTap a cell, then a digit below the grid. The eraser clears a cell. Switch to Notes to jot, small, the digits still possible in a cell.\n\n[fig:sudokuNotes] A cell in Notes mode: 1, 3 and 7 are still possible there.\n\nTap the selected cell again, or anywhere outside the grid, to deselect it. Digits given at the start can't be changed. The Hint button explains the next logical deduction: a digit to place, or notes to strike. If it needs notes, they are written for you."},
gLh(){return"Fill the grid so every row, every column and every box holds each digit exactly once: 1 to 4 on Easy's 4x4 grid, 1 to 9 on the 9x9 grids of the other levels.\n\n[fig:sudokuUnits] On a 4x4 grid, the ringed row, column and box each hold 1, 2, 3 and 4, once each.\n\n[fig:sudokuRepeat] Two 3s in the same row: not allowed. A 3 and a 1: allowed.\n\n[fig:sudokuSingle] The ringed cell sees a 1 in its row, a 2 in its column and a 4 in its box (shaded cells): it can only be a 3.\n\nPick a cell, then tap a digit to write it. Nothing is checked during play: you can erase or change a digit at any time.\n\nNotes mode lets you jot small digits in a cell without committing an answer.\n\n[fig:sudokuNotes] A cell in Notes mode: 1, 3 and 7 are still possible there.\n\nA finished grid scores points for every cell you filled, and a new one comes up at once.\n\nWhen time runs out, the grid in progress is checked cell by cell. A right digit scores points, a wrong one loses as many. A cell holding only notes is worth a share of the points if the right digit is among them, and loses as much otherwise: the more notes, the smaller the share. On a 9x9 grid, 3 notes are worth 6/9 of the points; noting all 9 digits is worth nothing."},
gZE(){return"Value"},
gZD(){return"Notes"},
gaog(){return"Records"},
glw(){return"\u2014"},
gXp(){return"Settings"},
gapd(){return"Appearance"},
gapc(){return"Light"},
gapb(){return"Dark"},
gape(){return"System"},
gakE(){return"Language"},
gWb(){return"Gameplay"},
gad6(){return"Rotate grid"},
gapP(){return"Vibration"},
alR(a){return""+a+" mines remaining"},
gadh(){return"Which symbol is the heaviest?"},
adg(a,b){return""+a+" symbols \u2022 "+b+" scales"},
Yn(a,b){return""+a+" digits \u2022 "+b+"s to look"},
gYo(){return"Memorize it"},
gYp(){return"Type what you saw"},
gYq(){return"Not quite \u2014 try again."},
aoJ(a,b){return""+a+" symbols \u2022 "+b+" ms/symbol"},
gaoK(){return"Memorize the sequence"},
gaoL(){return"Retype it in reverse"},
ajP(a,b,c){return""+a+"\u2013"+b+" symbols \u2022 "+A.jk(this.a).eS(c)+"s to look"},
gajT(){return"Memorize the grid"},
