guD(){return"Shikaku"},
gKO(){return"Cut the whole grid into rectangles. Each rectangle must contain exactly one number, and that number is its area (the count of cells inside). Rectangles never overlap, and together they cover every cell.\n\n[fig:shikakuWrong] Left, a rectangle holds two numbers: not allowed. Right, the rectangle around the 2 covers 4 cells: its area doesn't match its number.\n\nDrag from one corner to the opposite corner to draw a rectangle. Drag a corner or a side of a drawn rectangle to resize it, tap it to erase it; drawing over one replaces it. A rectangle can't hold two numbers, and one with no number or the wrong area turns red. The Hint button first gives what can be deduced straight from the grid; otherwise it reveals a rectangle's shape (horizontal, vertical or square), then, once every shape is known, the position of a rectangle."},
gKN(){return"Drag from corner to corner to draw a rectangle around a number, so that its area equals that number.\n\nEach rectangle holds exactly one number, and rectangles never overlap.\n\n[fig:shikakuWrong] Left, a rectangle holds two numbers: not allowed. Right, the rectangle around the 2 covers 4 cells: its area doesn't match its number.\n\nNothing is checked during play: draw, erase and redraw your rectangles freely. A rectangle whose area doesn't match its number shows in red, but a matching one isn't necessarily the solution's.\n\nA finished grid scores points for each of its numbers, and a new one comes up at once.\n\nWhen time runs out, the grid in progress is checked: each rectangle placed as in the solution scores points, each other rectangle loses as many. When in doubt, better to draw nothing."},
XE(a){var s=""+a
return s+"x"+s+" grid"},
guC(){return"Serpentin"},
gKH(){return"Draw one path that passes through every cell of the grid exactly once. It starts on 1, visits the numbers in order, and ends on the highest number.\n\nThe path moves from a cell to a neighbouring one \u2014 up, down, left or right. It never goes diagonally and never goes back through a cell it has already crossed.\n\n[fig:serpentinMoves] Allowed: onto a free neighbouring cell. Not allowed: diagonally (middle) or back onto the path (right).\n\nReaching the highest number isn't enough: the grid is only solved once the path has filled every cell.\n\n[fig:serpentinFill] Left, the path does end on 4 but leaves four cells empty: not solved. Right, it goes through every cell: solved.\n\nDrag from 1 to draw, cell by cell. Drag back over the path to shorten it, or tap a cell of the path to cut it back to there."},
gKG(){return"Draw a path from 1 through every cell of the grid, visiting the numbers in order and ending on the highest.\n\nThe path moves from a cell to a neighbouring one \u2014 up, down, left or right. It never goes diagonally and never goes back through a cell it has already crossed.\n\n[fig:serpentinMoves] Allowed: onto a free neighbouring cell. Not allowed: diagonally (middle) or back onto the path (right).\n\n[fig:serpentinFill] The path must fill the whole grid: ending on the last number with cells left empty (left) doesn't count.\n\nEach completed grid scores points for every one of its cells, and a new one is dealt at once.\n\nWhen time runs out, the path on the grid in progress is counted from the 1, cell by cell, as long as it follows the solution: each right cell scores points. The count stops at the first cell that strays from the solution, even if the rest of the path is right."},
X4(a){var s=""+a
return s+"x"+s+" grid"},
guB(){return"Sculptor"},
gKz(){return"A block of stone is cut into pieces. Break some of them to leave the silhouette pictured above the block.\n\n[fig:sculpteurGoal] The block (left) and the shape to carve (right).\n\nTap a piece to break it. Whatever rested on it falls, each piece dropping as one, until it lands on the floor or on another piece \u2014 so the order you break in matters.\n\n[fig:sculpteurFall] Breaking the piece marked with a cross: the one resting on it drops a cell, as one. Breaking the tall piece on the right then leaves the shape.\n\nUse undo to take a piece back. Only one choice of pieces gives the silhouette. The Hint button picks a piece at random and says whether it has to be broken (it is marked with a cross) or kept (it becomes unbreakable). If a piece was broken by mistake, it says how many moves to undo."},
gKy(){return"Break pieces off the block, and let what rests on them fall, to leave the silhouette pictured above it.\n\n[fig:sculpteurGoal] The block (left) and the shape to carve (right).\n\n[fig:sculpteurFall] Breaking a piece drops the one resting on it, as one.\n\nEach block carved scores points, and a new one is dealt at once. Keep going until time runs out."},
WI(a){var s=""+a
return s+"x"+s+" block"},
guv(){return"Mazecalc"},
gTG(){return'Every cell holds an operation. Draw a path from the top-left cell to the bottom-right cell, which shows the target as "=X". The path starts from the number in the top-left cell and applies each operation it crosses in turn: on reaching the last cell, the total must equal X. Only one path works. A path that reaches the last cell on any other total costs a 15-second penalty.\n\nSome cells also show a checkpoint "=Y" under their operation: the right path goes through them, with a total of Y after that cell. Checkpoints split the search into short stretches to work out one after the other.\n\nThe path moves one cell at a time, only right or down.\n\n[fig:labycalculMoves] Allowed: right or down. Not allowed: back up or left (middle), or diagonally (right).\n\nDrag from the top-left cell to draw. Drag back over the path to shorten it, or tap a cell of the path to cut it back to there. The Hint button outlines the cell where a wrong path leaves the route, or the next step, and tells you the total.'},
gTF(){return'Draw a path from the top-left cell to the bottom-right one, moving only right or down, whose operations make the target shown in the last cell ("=X"). Cells marked "=Y" are checkpoints: the right path goes through them with a total of Y.\n\n[fig:labycalculMoves] Allowed: right or down. Not allowed: up, left or diagonally.\n\nA path that lands on the target scores points for each of its cells, and a new grid is dealt at once. A path that reaches the last cell on any other total loses a few points: go back and keep working on the grid. Keep going until time runs out.'},
